## Quickstart

```bash
uv lock                      # creates uv.lock; commit it (pinned, reproducible environment)
uv sync --extra dev --frozen
uv run pytest                # verification suite
uv run ruff check . && uv run ruff format --check . && uv run mypy
uv run @@PROJECT_NAME@@ run --config config/default.toml --output-dir outputs
```

Without `uv`: `python -m venv .venv && . .venv/bin/activate && pip install -e '.[dev]'`.

## Assumptions and validity range

State every assumption here before trusting a result. Each row needs a regime of validity and
a check that would reveal its violation. Keep this table in sync with `docs/design-notes.md`.

| ID | Assumption | Valid when | Violation check |
|----|------------|-----------|-----------------|
| A1 | Linear restoring force F = -k x | amplitude small versus the spring's nonlinear range | residual structure in fit; amplitude scan |
| A2 | Viscous damping F = -c v | low Reynolds number, no dry friction | log-decrement independent of amplitude |
| A3 | Point mass, no spring mass | spring mass << m | repeat with effective-mass correction |
| A4 | SI units throughout; names carry units (`_kg`, `_m`, `_s`) | always | `tests/test_units.py` |

(Replace these rows with your model's assumptions. Unlisted assumptions are a defect.)

