## Layout

```text
src/@@PACKAGE@@/   typed headless core (model, solver, analytic, uncertainty, comparison, provenance)
config/            data, never code; units in key names
docs/adr/          architecture decision records (stack, paradigm, interface)
docs/              design notes and verification plan
tests/             unit, dimensional, convergence, conservation, property, architecture tests
```

Interfaces (`cli.py`, and `gui/` if generated) are thin callers of the core; a test forbids
the core from importing them or any GUI toolkit.

## Reproducibility

Each run writes `results.json` and `trajectory.csv` (byte-identical for the same config and
seed) plus `run_metadata.json` (timestamp, git commit, Python and dependency versions, config
and input hashes, seed). Commit `uv.lock`; metadata records its hash when present.

## Limitations

- The reference model is a linear damped oscillator used to demonstrate the engineering
  scaffold only.
- Tooling (ruff, mypy, pytest-cov, Pint, hypothesis) is declared in `pyproject.toml`; install
  it with the quickstart and run the checks before relying on the CI configuration.
